<title>THAILAND: Thai stock market closed for Buddhist holiday.</title>
<headline>Thai stock market closed for Buddhist holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET) was closed on Friday for a Buddhist religious holiday.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the SET Index gained 15.96 points, or 2.18 percent, to close at 747.70 on trade worth 9.35 billion baht. The SET-50 index rose 2.77 percent, or 1.50 points, to 55.57.</p>
<p>The market will reopen on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
